<section class="section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <h2 class="heading">Where Notes sits</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Notepad++ is fast, but it hasn't kept up — no real markdown, no quick-open.
      Obsidian and VS Code are powerful, but they want a vault or a workspace
      before you've typed a word. Notes sits in the gap: modern conveniences,
      none of the ceremony.
    </p>

    <div class="spectrum" role="img" aria-label="A spectrum from fast-but-dated on the left to powerful-but-heavy on the right, with Notes positioned toward the fast end">
      <div class="spectrum-labels">
        <span>Notepad++</span>
        <span>Obsidian / VS Code</span>
      </div>
      <div class="spectrum-track">
        <div class="spectrum-marker" style="left: 32%">
          <span class="marker-dot"></span>
          <span class="marker-label">Notes</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="spectrum-captions">
        <span>fast, dated</span>
        <span>powerful, heavy</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="closer">
      No vault. No index database. No project config required to start typing.
      Point Notes at a file and it's already yours — open a folder alongside it
      only if you want a view into what else is there.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

